WEBVTT

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.710
Here is...

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.630
I...

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.560
How did I get back to my room?

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:48.730
I see; I managed to endure and get past it.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:50.980
I'm glad.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:55.570
Kizunairo kokoro to kokoro

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:55.570
The color of bonds binding hearts to hearts

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:58.780
Yakusoku no basho kitto michibiku wa

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:58.780
Will surely lead us to the Promised Land.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:03.040
Tsutaetai tsutaekirenai

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:03.040
I want to tell you, but I can't.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:07.040
Hatenai omoi ha anata...

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:07.040
I always long for you...

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:17.470
Boukansha no hibi ni yuuki wo dashitara sayonara

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:17.470
Say goodbye to the days of just being a bystander.

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:26.520
Demo "jiyuu" no teigi ni buranko no you ni yureteru no ne?

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:26.520
But am I swaying over the meaning of "Freedom", like a swing?

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:31.650
Gosenfu ni kaita kaidan

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:31.650
Stairs drawn on a music score,

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:35.150
Ippo susunde niho sagattemo

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:35.150
Even if I go down one step and back two steps,

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:39.160
Honno chotto setsunasa utau

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:39.160
The notes play a sad melody.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:42.200
Watashi no real kanjite ne

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:42.200
Hear my reality!

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:46.120
Kizunairo kokoro to kokoro

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:46.120
The color of bonds binding hearts to hearts

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:49.670
Yakusoku no basho kitto michibikuwa

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:49.670
Will surely lead us to the Promised Land.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:53.630
Tsutaetai tsutaekirenai

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:53.630
I want to tell you, but can't

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:57.050
Zutto anata wo sagashiteta

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:57.050
I've always been searching for you.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:01.140
Tatoeba sou anataga hikari

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:01.140
Let's say you are the light

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:04.600
Watashi ga kagede mitsume aetanara

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:04.600
And I'm the shadow, gazing at one other.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.640
Namida iro no diamond

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.640
The tear-colored diamond

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.440
Nee zero kara kagayakasetai

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.440
I want to make it shine from nothing.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:17.990
Kowagaranaide musunde ne ai wo

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:17.990
Don't be afraid of falling in love.

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:20.160
Deaiwo...

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:20.160
Nor of meeting people...

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:26.250
Parting

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:26.740
Hey there, Boss.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:29.450
I've got something I wanted to ask you.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:31.830
Sure, I'll be right with you when I'm done with this.

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:34.830
Getting reference materials together took longer than expected.

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:37.630
Shiro, can you make some tea?

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:39.380
Nii-san, where's the list from last year?

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:41.710
Looks like we're all set with supplies.

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:47.340
Thanks to Hasekura-kun creating ties with
the shopping district, things might go smoother this year.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.810
You look especially cheerful.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:53.390
Did something good happen?

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:54.520
Something good?

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:56.190
You could say that.

00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:01.110
Nii-san, I think I can keep myself out of her manipulation.

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:03.820
Really?

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:07.240
Good morning.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.280
Hasekura-kun, you're late.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:11.280
I was waiting for you.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:13.620
Here's the reference materials you asked for.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:15.790
Thank you. I'll take them.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:20.750
What's this?

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:23.130
Senpai?

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.130
Vice Prez? What's wrong?

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:27.550
Hasekura-kun...

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:37.180
Could this be...

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.480
No! Let go of me!

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:40.480
Why?

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:42.900
Vice Prez!

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:04.170
Hasekura-kun... What have you done...

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:07.630
Vice Prez.

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:08.550
Don't come near me.

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:11.220
I'm fine.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:13.760
I'm just fine.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:16.970
Thank you.

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:21.150
You saved me.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:23.110
Really?

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:24.900
Y-Yes.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:31.030
Oh yeah. Could you help me organize the reference materials?

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:32.450
S-Sure.

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:34.870
Categorize it for me.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:37.080
Have a seat there.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:40.460
Let's make a list categorized by year.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.790
Is something wrong with Erika-senpai?

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:48.840
She looked strange the moment Hasekura-senpai came in.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:50.760
It's nothing you need to concern yourself with, Shiro.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.300
But...

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.430
Sei's right.

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:58.390
This is a problem between Erika and Hasekura-kun.

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:00.770
Between them?

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:04.110
I'd say the time has come.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:06.820
There's nothing we can do.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:07.940
You don't mean...

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:11.530
Could I have another cup?

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.780
Man, I'm hungry.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.740
I'll have the B-Set.

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:17.330
At this rate, we're not going to finish in time.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:19.620
Should we ask for help from our club members?

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:24.330
Vice Prez said she's all right, but...

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:26.460
Is something on your mind?

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:30.170
No surprise. It's only going to get worse.

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:32.300
What's going to get worse?

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:34.930
Kouhei, locked on!

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:42.730
Where did you go yesterday, leaving Hina-chan and me alone?

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:47.400
Sendo-san was missing partway through, too, so were you...

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:51.280
No, no. Vice Prez and I aren't like that.

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:53.150
Really?

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:54.610
If you're lying to us...

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:57.120
I'm telling the truth.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.990
It's hard being so popular.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.580
Then what <i>were</i> you doing?

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:06.460
The fireworks!

00:06:06.460 --> 00:06:10.630
The fireworks gave me a good idea, so we started to...

00:06:10.630 --> 00:06:12.510
"The fireworks"?

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:15.050
I get it! For the after party!

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:19.390
Fireworks are a must for the greatest closing events.

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:21.390
The folk dance is a must, too.

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:23.810
So what are you going to do with the fireworks?

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:29.110
I-I think I'll keep it to myself until it's fleshed out a little more.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:32.070
Okay. Feel free to ask me for anything when you're stuck.

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:33.360
Yeah. Thank you.

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:37.740
I've got to concentrate on the work in front of me.

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:42.540
For the Vice Prez's sake, too.

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:44.250
No...

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.960
Blood's not working!

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:53.300
None of this is doing the job.

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:57.930
What... What I want is...

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:08.230
It's not Hasekura-kun's fault.

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:09.690
But...

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:15.400
Why... Hasekura-kun...

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:19.250
Heiji, give me that.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:20.620
No!

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:22.790
Come on!

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.470
Everyone's working hard.

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:32.640
This place is good.

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:39.980
Ah, Vice Pre-

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:40.640
Oh, Boss!

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:43.560
Perfect timing. Could you come here for a second?

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:46.320
Sure.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:50.490
This part here. We couldn't get the stuff we needed.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:54.200
Oh. Then I'll ask the people from the shopping district later.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:55.950
Thank you.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:57.950
You're amazing. Thank you.

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:00.500
Good morning!

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.580
Ah, good morning.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:05.880
Good morning.

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:09.380
Hasekura.

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:11.670
Do you mind lending me a hand?

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:12.880
Sure, no problem.

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:58.930
Vice-President

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:13.150
Hasekura-kun...

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:24.000
No... If I see Hasekura-kun now, I'll...

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:31.300
How long do you think clutching that will work?

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:43.520
Kuze Kiriha?

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:51.820
The blood of Hasekura Kouhei is special.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:57.030
Moreover, he's starting to become someone precious to you.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:06.160
Once you drink his blood, the thirst for his blood will become greater, and soon you won't be able to resist it.

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:10.170
You should understand that very well right now.

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.380
Here's a message from her.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:16.260
"Why do you hesitate for a person who willingly gave his blood?"

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:20.300
"Why won't you make Hasekura Kouhei your Dependent?"

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:23.970
So you are...

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:27.680
I see. You've returned to being with my mother.

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:32.020
"If you have no intention of taking a Dependent, return to the mansion at once."

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:34.270
Kaya said that.

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:38.070
What?! But I still have time before graduation!

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:42.450
She's breaking her promise.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:45.790
That was time given to you to find a Dependent.

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:49.000
If you refuse to take a Dependent, then the promise, itself, is equivalent to not existing.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.460
Don't be so selfish!

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:54.250
No matter what she says, I won't take a Dependent!

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:58.340
Before graduation, I will find a different way to live!

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:02.550
Why are you so stubborn over this matter?

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:04.600
You don't wish to cease this?

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:07.060
I don't want to hear that from Mother's toy.

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:13.270
Why did you choose to return to her?

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:16.980
She'll take away your memories again one day.

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:23.030
And she's going to make you find
your master without any idea of who it is!

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:37.000
You spend decades, centuries, finding her,
only for her to take your memories away again.

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.590
Then starts another round of endless games.

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:43.390
Just how long have you been doing this?

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:45.300
Why did you return to her?!

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:50.770
It's because that's what Kaya wishes.

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:56.270
I can't disobey my master's orders.

00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:59.610
Exactly.

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:03.360
To a Dependent, the Master's orders are absolute.

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:08.910
They'll do everything word-for-word, even the tiniest mumble.

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:14.080
I'm scared of the darkness in my heart.

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:21.380
I'm scared of what I may ask of Hasekura-kun if I take him as a Dependent.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:25.720
I want to live as a human.

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:28.470
That's why I won't take a Dependent!

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:30.770
I won't become like my Mother!

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:35.480
I understand your point.

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:39.020
But you can't fight your fate.

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:42.490
Think hard.

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:56.460
Hase... kura... kun...

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:19.400
What was that?!

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:23.150
Owie.

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:25.530
Are you okay, Onee-chan?

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:28.530
G-Good morning, Kouhei.

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:31.540
It's raining hard, isn't it?

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:37.960
So I wanted to hang these teruteru-bozu to get the sun out,
in hopes that preparations will go smoothly.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:40.590
And why does that bring you to my balcony?

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:44.630
It might be more effective hanging from the head organizer's balcony.

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:46.470
Oh please, Kanade-san...

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:47.720
Relax.

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:52.680
We were able to have a tea party after so long, so let's let it slide.

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:58.100
Yeah. We haven't had a chance to have a tea party with all the Culture Festival preparations going on.

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:00.770
How about we call Eririn down, too?

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:03.400
You'll only be bothering her so early in the morning.

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:08.530
She must be tired from the daily grind, so we should let her sleep.

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:10.950
I'm tired, too, you know.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:14.410
Not on the same level as Eririn!

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:19.000
Oh yeah. What ever happened to the after party event?

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.210
Did your idea come together?

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:24.090
Ah, to be honest, not at all.

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:27.920
It should be something everyone can have fun with.

00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:32.930
Something we can have dreams about and remember forever.

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:35.720
It'd be nice if it can have something you can take home!

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:38.770
Hey! Don't say too many things at once.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:40.270
You're right.

00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:45.610
You can't come up with great ideas like that so easily.

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:48.200
That's it! That's a great idea.

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:53.910
Vice Prez!

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:58.000
What's the big rush?

00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:59.410
Well...

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:04.880
The Vice Prez isn't here again?

00:15:06.510 --> 00:15:09.010
Well, she's...

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:12.930
I had Erika go talk to the shopping district first thing in the morning.

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:15.680
The shopping district? All by herself?

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:20.560
You're right. I probably should have had you go with her.

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:22.850
Silly me.

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:25.860
Did you need her for something?

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:30.450
I've got an idea for the after party ready, so I wanted her to take a look at it.

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:32.110
What is that?

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:34.120
Parachute of happiness.

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:36.030
Parachute of happiness?

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:39.960
Yeah. I was thinking about launching this with the fireworks.

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:47.380
Don't you think it'll be interesting if we say a wish comes true if you find this, like the Hosaka Zelkova?

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:53.720
It'll be a good memory from the festival, and I think it would keep the feeling from the day forever.

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:56.850
That sounds very romantic.

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:58.310
Do you think it's a little childish?

00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:00.430
No, I don't think so at all.

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:03.020
I'm sure Erika-senpai will like it, too.

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:05.810
I hope she will.

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:13.360
She always prioritizes the students having fun over herself as a member of the Student Council, right?

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:20.580
That's why I want her to at least enjoy the after party
as a student of the Shuchikan Academy.

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:24.040
Hasekura-senpai.

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:26.960
Could you give this to the Vice Prez for me?

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:28.750
Yes.

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:30.670
Um!

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:31.630
Shiro.

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:33.510
Yes...

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:43.230
Erika-senpai.

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:51.070
Erika-senpai, is it all right?

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:55.070
I'm fine. I feel better than I have been.

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:59.330
No, that's not what I meant.

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:02.080
I was wondering if you were all right with keeping things the way they are.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:04.830
Hasekura-kun...

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:11.130
Senpai!

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:16.760
There's no good or bad to this now.

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:20.310
She's down on the table just from thinking about him.

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:28.060
If they were to meet now, I'm sure Erika will lose control and attack his neck.

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:34.280
If she does, her desire for his blood will grow.

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:36.740
Stop it...

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:40.410
It's not a problem while you're being fed blood.

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:42.950
But sadly, he's a human.

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:45.410
He'll eventually die of old age.

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:49.380
Stop it...

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:57.010
Submitting to the fear of eventually losing him, you will-

00:17:57.010 --> 00:17:58.340
Stop it!

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:04.930
Senpai.

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:07.270
But this is reality.

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:12.690
We, the Sendos, and humans have lived many years just like that.

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:15.190
That's our fate.

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:16.610
Fate...

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:20.740
Why?! Isn't there any way around this?

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:25.290
Isn't there a way for Hasekura-senpai and Erika-senpai be together like they used to?

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:30.670
Perhaps if there's a blood donor to replace Hasekura-kun.

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:33.630
Oh, but his blood is special.

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:36.210
It can't be just anyone off the street.

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:45.600
It can't be me?

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:52.690
Kuchiduketa akai yakusoku

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:52.690
The red promise sealed with a kiss.

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:49.100
What?

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:51.730
Shiro?

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:59.320
Tsumasaki de kimi dake ni ageruyo

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:59.320
On my toes, I'll only give it to you.

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:55.730
I will become Erika-senpai's Dependent.

00:18:55.730 --> 00:19:00.910
If I do, Hasekura-senpai won't have to become a Dependent, right?

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:05.990
Mabushii hikari nara ima ha iranaiwa

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:05.990
I don't need the bright light now

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:06.290
Shiro, do you understand what you're saying?

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:11.120
Futari ga isshoni ireba

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:11.120
If we can be together.

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:10.210
Do you not like me, Erika-senpai?

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:13.460
Wouldn't you like me as your Dependent?

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:16.380
That's not what I'm saying.

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:20.340
Becoming a Dependent means you'll no longer be human.

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:26.310
But it hurts...

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:30.190
Watching Erika-senpai suffer so much...

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:33.150
Nurui nemuri zutto matteta

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:33.150
I've been waiting for this warm, soothing sleep.

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:35.360
Watching Hasekura-senpai working so hard without knowing what's going on.

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:39.900
Me wo samashinasai kodou odayakani

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:39.900
Open your eyes to a steady heartbeat.

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:38.530
Shiro, don't say such ridiculous things.

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:39.690
No!

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:46.370
Inori to sotto rizumu ni awaseta

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:46.370
I've synchronized my prayer to its rhythm.

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:44.280
If it's the fate of the Sendos to have Dependents,

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:49.160
then it's the fate and duty of the Togis to serve the Sendos.

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:54.040
Kako ha atarashii kyou no tame no kiseki

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:54.040
The past is a guide to the arising today.

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:51.620
Shiro...

00:19:54.040 --> 00:20:00.630
Nukumori ga netsu wo obiteku

00:19:54.040 --> 00:20:00.630
The warmth is starting to build up.

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:00.800
Iori! You!

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:07.220
Watashi kara yubisaki wo kasaneta

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:07.220
I took the initiative and laid my fingers on yours.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:03.720
What is this?!

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:05.680
You never said anything like this could happen!

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:08.100
Don't get so worked up, Sei.

00:20:07.220 --> 00:20:13.900
Yasashii kimochi hora zenbu agerukara

00:20:07.220 --> 00:20:13.900
I'll give you all my tender heart.

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:10.890
Just like you care for Shiro-chan,

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:15.610
I only wanted Erika to find her path in life.

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:20.400
Waratte waratte douka

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:20.400
Please smile. Please smile.

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:17.270
Nii-san...

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:20.900
Let go of me, Sei.

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:25.870
Souyo yakusoku ha

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:25.870
A promise is

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:24.490
Let go.

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:33.750
"Mamoranakya ikenai mono" nankajya nakute

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:33.750
Not "something that needs to be kept".

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:34.670
Nii-san... Did you bring Hasekura-kun to the
Student Council knowing this would happen?

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:39.130
Kitto yakusoku ha

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:39.130
A promise will

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:39.090
There's no such thing as a big brother who doesn't wish for a happy life for his cute little sister.

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:41.090
How could you?

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:47.510
"Mamoru koto kimeta toki" taisetsu ni naruno

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:47.510
Becomes important "the moment you decide it needs to be kept".

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:44.130
Don't worry.

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:49.310
No matter what happens, I won't do anything that would take your future away.

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:53.480
I will decide my own path in life!

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:58.150
Zeitaku na tsuki no yoru

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:58.150
On a night with a wondrous moon,

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:04.150
Futari ha tada yorisou

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:04.150
The couple will simply lean on each other.

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:04.950
Erika-senpai will be happy, too, eh?

00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:10.830
Fushigi dayone koushite ireba

00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:10.830
How strange. Just doing this

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:11.540
Let's be sure to make the Culture Festival a great one, Vice Prez.

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:16.710
Fuansae mo kiete yuku

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:16.710
Erases all worries.

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:18.080
Hasekura Kouhei

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:16.000
Hasekura-kun...

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:23.800
Subete ha kono hi no tameni

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:23.800
Everything is for this day.

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:30.010
Subete ha kono hi no tameni...

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:38.060
I'm sorry... I don't think I can hold myself back anymore.

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:37.900
Waratte waratte douka

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:37.900
Please smile. Please smile.

00:21:37.900 --> 00:21:50.830
Waratte waratte douka...

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:42.360
Thank you so much...

00:21:56.040 --> 00:22:03.380
I miss you

00:22:13.850 --> 00:22:23.480
Mabushii kurai e ni kaita jikan nano

00:22:13.850 --> 00:22:23.480
Just like in a perfect painting,

00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:28.240
Sou ima ha...

00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:28.240
Now is a dazzling moment.

00:22:32.530 --> 00:22:42.290
Kawari hajimeta machinami ni me wo sorashi

00:22:32.530 --> 00:22:42.290
I look away from the city that's starting to change

00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:48.010
Omoide ha tada iuno

00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:48.010
And my memories whisper to me, saying,

00:22:48.010 --> 00:22:55.140
Soko de tomadou dake

00:22:48.010 --> 00:22:55.140
You're only at a loss.

00:22:55.140 --> 00:22:57.140
I miss you

00:22:57.140 --> 00:23:01.400
Omoi wo sono mama dakishimete

00:22:57.140 --> 00:23:01.400
Hold on to your feelings.

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:03.310
I miss you

00:23:03.310 --> 00:23:07.650
Kawaranu omoi wo shiritai no

00:23:03.310 --> 00:23:07.650
I want to know how you've always felt.

00:23:07.650 --> 00:23:09.530
I miss you

00:23:09.530 --> 00:23:13.280
Negatteru kara

00:23:09.530 --> 00:23:13.280
I'll always long for you, so...

00:23:13.830 --> 00:23:19.290
I miss you...

00:23:44.150 --> 00:23:48.150
So this is your answer?

00:23:55.070 --> 00:23:57.240
Hasekura Kouhei, eh?

00:23:58.160 --> 00:24:01.660
I still have high hopes for you, you know.

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:20.980
Twelfth Episode

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:20.980
「Red Promise」

00:24:07.550 --> 00:24:08.760
Good morning.

00:24:08.760 --> 00:24:10.090
Have a good day.

00:24:10.880 --> 00:24:11.970
I'm home.

00:24:12.930 --> 00:24:14.220
Good night.

00:24:14.220 --> 00:24:16.010
Everyday life.

00:24:17.180 --> 00:24:18.930
The promise between the two.
